# AMD64 thunk export spec -- setupapi.dll.
#
# Added from the 2026-08-15 first-real-game triage: with the application's own
# shipped DLLs now loadable (find_dll_file() searches the load path for the
# guest's machine instead of refusing it outright), what stopped
# quake2ex_steam.exe was Wine builtins with no guest thunk -- each reported as
# c000007b, the loader correctly refusing to splice a native ppc64 module into
# a guest call.  Nothing here is hand-written: the export list comes from this
# module's own .spec.
DLL setupapi.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# The module's first .spec-location downgrade, from the 2026-08-30
# ahead-of-time sweep (import_chain.py over every installed title).  Oblivion
# Remastered imports SetupGetInfDriverStoreLocationW statically; the generator
# refuses it as "no declaration found in Wine headers" and the name is indeed
# declared nowhere under include/, so the .spec is the only pin available.
#
# Return kind justified against the implementation: dlls/setupapi/query.c:691
# is BOOL WINAPI.  Arity six, from setupapi.spec's own
# (wstr ptr wstr ptr long ptr); every argument is pointer or integer class.
SetupGetInfDriverStoreLocationW  0x00000C01  6  int   setupapi.spec:443
